.TH PDFCUBE 1 "October 2026" "pdfcube 0.1.0" "PDFCube Manual"
.SH NAME
pdfcube \- present PDF slides with animated 3D transitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfcube
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ presentation.pdf ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfcube
is a focused PDF presentation viewer with animated cube transitions,
programmed slide timing, and keyboard-controlled zoom regions. Pages are
rendered with Poppler and Cairo and displayed through GTK 4 and OpenGL.
.PP
If no PDF file is supplied, a file chooser is displayed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the PDFCube version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bgcolor " " r:g:b"
Set the background color. Each component is a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-top-color " " r:g:b"
Set the cube cap color. Each component is a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no-fullscreen
Start in a window instead of fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Automatically advance slides using PDF transition durations or the program
specified with
.BR \-\-program .
.TP
.BI \-\-program " n:x:n:x:..."
Set slide durations and following transition types. Durations are in seconds;
.B c
selects a cube transition and
.B p
selects a plain transition. The last pair is repeated for remaining slides.
For example,
.B \-\-program 5:c:3:p
uses five seconds followed by a cube, then three seconds followed by a plain
transition.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.TP
.B Space, Page Down
Advance using the programmed transition.
.TP
.B c, a
Move forward or backward with a cube transition.
.TP
.B Right, Left, Page Up
Move forward or backward without animation.
.TP
.B h, j, k, l, z
Zoom into predefined regions.
.TP
.B g
Reset the zoom.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B t
Toggle automatic advancement.
.TP
.B 1 through 9
Jump to page 5*(n-1). These unmodified keys are page shortcuts.
.TP
.B Ctrl-1 through Ctrl-9
Jump to the corresponding PDF or programmed cube section. The Ctrl modifier
keeps section navigation distinct from the page shortcuts above.
.TP
.B Ctrl-l
Reload the OpenGL resources and redraw.
.TP
.B Escape, Ctrl-q
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Options may be placed in
.IR ~/.pdfcuberc
using Boost Program Options syntax. Command-line options take precedence.
For example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
demo=true
bgcolor=0:0:0
program=5:p
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pdfcube slides.pdf
Present a PDF in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B pdfcube --demo --program 5:c slides.pdf
Advance every five seconds with cube transitions.
.TP
.B pdfcube --no-fullscreen --bgcolor 0:0:0 slides.pdf
Present in a window with a black background.
